ouncing embattled Greg Schiano would return as coach for a 19th season, the Scarlet Knights stunned Penn State 25-24 Saturday, their first win over the Nittany Lions since 1988, and just their third this year.","published":"2026-11-22T02:37:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50557643/rutgers-authors-special-win-1st-penn-state-1988","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Notre Dame loses safety Luke Talich to injury in first quarter vs. SMU","description":"Notre Dame starting safety Luke Talich left the Fighting Irish's game against SMU in the first quarter with an apparent right leg injury suffered on the opening drive of the game Saturday night in South Bend, Indiana.","published":"2026-11-22T02:00:01.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556999/notre-dame-safety-luke-talich-exits-1st-half-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Which teams have the best odds to make the College Football Playoff?","description":"We are tracking the odds for making the CFP, earning a bye and winning it all.","published":"2026-11-22T01:42:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Brandon's two TD runs lift No. 9 Tennessee past LSU","description":"Tennessee's stifling defense shut down LSU, and the No. 9 Volunteers beat the Tigers 27-13 on Saturday to maintain their place in the College Football Playoff hunt.","published":"2026-11-22T01:48:32.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556758/brandon-two-td-runs-lift-no-9-tennessee-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bryce Underwood makes most of second chance, sparks Michigan's upset of UCLA","description":"Reinserted as Michigan's starting quarterback earlier this week, Bryce Underwood threw a 3-yard 2-point conversion pass Jalen Hoffman, lifting the Wolverines to an 18-16 triple-overtime win over previously unbeaten No. 4 UCLA on Saturday night.","published":"2026-11-22T01:36:46.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556702/bryce-underwood-michigan-outlast-ucla-triple-over","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Nebraska's jab at Ohio State's 'THE' leads top Week 12 CFB trolls","description":"Nebraska deployed a simple but effective troll that poked fun at its opponent's propensity to emphasize the \"the\" in \"The Ohio State University.\"","published":"2026-11-22T01:12:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50554531/nebraska-ohio-state-trolls-college-football-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana's CFP hopes take hit after OT loss at Washington","description":"Indiana might not get a chance to defend its national championship after losing 27-24 at Washington on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T02:30:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556327/indiana-cfp-hopes-take-hit-ot-loss-washington","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"UCLA loses Ty Dieffenbach to injury, stays resolute with B1G title game in reach","description":"UCLA coach Bob Chesney said his message to the Bruins was, \"Nobody hang your head,\" despite losing QB Ty Dieffenbach to injury in a tough, 18-16 defeat at Michigan on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T02:41:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556107/ucla-qb-ty-dieffenbach-carted-3ot-loss-michigan","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 live: Tracking top moments and best highlights","description":"Tracking the top plays and developments from Week 12.","published":"2026-11-22T00:47:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50541394/week-12-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Preseason No. 1 Ohio State suffers fourth loss, will 'evaluate what's going on'","description":"For coach Ryan Day and his Ohio State Buckeyes, the dream of a College Football Playoff run is dead, as the preseason No. 1 team in college football lost its fourth game on Saturday afternoon, a 31-28 decision at the hands of the Nebraska Cornhuskers.","published":"2026-11-22T00:30:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50555411/preseason-no-1-ohio-state-sees-cfp-hopes-end-4th-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5081821/kenyatta-jackson-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenyatta_Jackson"},"pick":{"pick":54,"round":2,"team":"NYG","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Kenyatta Jackson","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenyatta_Jackson","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-18T13:13:47Z","intro":"Kenyatta Jackson Jr. (born February 11, 2004) is an American college football defensive end for the Ohio State Buckeyes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Jackson attended Chaminade–Madonna College Preparatory School located in Hollywood, Florida. During his senior season, he totaled 55 tackles, 17 tackles for loss, 15 quarter back hurries and 14 sacks, where for his performance he was named the Florida Gatorade Player of the Year. Coming out of high school, Jackson was rated as a four-star recruit, the 7th overall defensive end, and the 78th overall player in the class of 2022, where he committed to play college football for the Ohio State Buckeyes over offers from other schools such as Alabama, Auburn, Clemson, Florida, Florida State, Georgia Tech, Miami, North Carolina, Nebraska, Oklahoma, Oregon, and Penn State."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Heading into his true freshman season in 2022, Jackson lost his black stripe before the start of the season, where he chose to wear the jersey #97, which Ohio State greats like Joey Bosa, Nick Bosa, and Cameron Heyward all wore. In his freshman season in 2022 he recorded just two tackles. During the 2023 season, Jackson notched seven tackles with two being for a loss and a sack and a half. He finished the 2024 season, playing in all 16 games, recording 15 tackles and a sack and a half, as he helped the Buckeyes win the 2025 National Championship."}]}}